# Build artifacts
*.obj
*.OBJ
*.o
*.lib
*.LIB
*.EXE
*.exe
# Exception: Clark's original reference binaries (tracked byte-exact)
!pcb1541/pcbic12/bin/*.EXE
!pcb1541/pcbic12/bin/*.exe
!pcb1541/install/reference/*.EXE

# NOTE: toolkit/pplc/ holds NO compiler binaries by design.
# !toolkit/pplc/**/*.EXE was added to track a PPLC320.EXE that was never
# committed and does not belong there — toolkit/pplc/<ver>/out/ is for
# compiled .PPE output. Per toolkit/pplc/README.md the decision is to
# build PPLC from Clark's source, not extract the shipped binaries;
# Clark's PPLC320.EXE stays inside
# reference/roysac/PCB1522-CS2BACKUP-Clean.ZIP. Compiler distributions
# live in devtools/. Rule removed rather than left whitelisting an
# empty location.

# Exception: OUT/clark-original — Clark's shipped 15.4 beta binaries.
# Reference material, NOT our build output. These were lost once already:
# tracked at OUT/DOS/ and OUT/OS2/, then the *.EXE rule above landed, the
# 2026-08-25 restructure deleted them, and nothing flagged the absence
# because git could no longer see them. Keep them tracked.
!OUT/clark-original/**/*.EXE
!OUT/clark-original/**/*.exe

# Exception: PCBIC v1.2 binaries in the 15.4 PWA output slot.
# Byte-exact reconstruction, kept as the released reference.
!OUT/upd154/*.EXE
!OUT/upd154/*.exe

# Exception: OUT/delta154 — the 15.4 Delta Watcom build (_W suffix).
# Released artifacts, tracked deliberately: they were committed at
# bin/watcom/ from 2026-08-08, deleted in the 2026-08-25 restructure
# (e4181e5) and never re-added, while DELTA154-CHANGES.md went on
# claiming "15 EXEs in OUT/delta154/". Nothing flagged it because the
# *.EXE rule hid the absence — the same way Clark's binaries were lost
# in the same commit. Keep them visible to git.
!OUT/delta154/*.EXE
!OUT/delta154/*.exe

# Exception: OUT/pwa153 — the 15.3 PWA build (Borland C++ 3.1).
# Built from source 2026-09-16 via Clark's own COMPILE.BAT/PCBOARD.MAK.
# Released artifacts; see OUT/pwa153/BUILD-RECIPE.md.
!OUT/pwa153/*.EXE
!OUT/pwa153/*.exe

# Exception: the SDK and category libraries.
# *.LIB is ignored as build output above, but these are released SDK /
# link-input artifacts and must stay visible to git. OUT/lib/ was deleted
# on 2026-09-17 and its rules removed with it. Both the SDK and the
# category libraries now live under toolkit/<branch>/<compiler>/lib/ —
# they come from the same tree and the same compiler. OUT/pwa153/lib/
# was retired on 2026-09-17; do not recreate it.
#
# Keep these visible. Twice now, artifacts have been lost because an
# ignore rule hid their absence from git: Clark's 15.4 beta binaries and
# the 15 Watcom _W builds, both in the 2026-08-25 restructure.
!toolkit/**/lib/*.LIB
!toolkit/**/lib/*.lib
!toolkit/**/lib/*.LST
!toolkit/**/lib/*.386

# Local reverse-engineering scratch — one working folder at repo root,
# named by archive under /analysis/<archive>/. Never tracked.
# Explicit patterns cover the dir + everything under it (belt-and-suspenders).
/analysis/
/analysis/**
/analysis/*/
/analysis/*/*
*.MAP
*.map
*.ERR
*.err
*.i
*.lst

# Temp/backup
*~
*.bak
*.BAK
!attic/*.BAK
!attic/*.bak
*.tmp
*.TMP
*.swp
*.orig

# Third-party (clone separately)
OS2TK/
codebase-dbf/

# Large archives (available separately)
#pcb153src0014.zip
#pcb15everything.zip

# IDE/editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*

# Allow built binaries
!tools/qfront/bin/dos/*.exe
!tools/qfront/bin/dos/*.EXE
!bin/*.exe
!bin/*.EXE
!PCBSRC/MAIN/SOURCE/UTIL/*/*.exe
!PCBSRC/MAIN/SOURCE/UTIL/*/*.EXE
!dist/*.exe
!dist/*.EXE
!dist/*.ZIP
!dist/*.zip
!attic/*.exe
!attic/*.EXE
!attic/*.ZIP
!attic/*.zip


# Allow extracted-installer parity binaries under target/
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.EXE
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.exe
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.COM
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.com
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.DLL
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.dll
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.BIN
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.bin

# Allow extracted-installer parity list files under target/
# (needed because *.lst above matches case-insensitively on Windows/macOS Git,
#  which would otherwise silently drop BLT.LST, DIR.LST, DLPATH.LST files)
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.LST
!pcb1541/install/dist/target/**/*.lst

# ===========================================================================
# LAST WORD — tracked artifacts, re-asserted at the end of the file.
#
# In .gitignore the LAST matching rule wins. Exceptions written next to the
# thing they describe are fragile: a later broad rule silently re-ignores
# them, and this file is long enough that nobody notices. That is how the
# project lost Clark's 15.4 beta binaries and the 15 Watcom _W builds in a
# single commit.
#
# Everything that must stay visible to git is repeated HERE, after every
# ignore rule in the file. Add new exceptions here, not only inline.
# ===========================================================================

# Clark's shipped 15.4 beta binaries (reference, not our output)
!OUT/clark-original/**/*.EXE
!OUT/clark-original/**/*.exe

# 15.3 PWA build output
!OUT/pwa153/*.EXE
!OUT/pwa153/*.exe

# PCBIC v1.2 binaries on the 15.4 PWA leg
!OUT/pwa153/upd154/*.EXE
!OUT/pwa153/upd154/*.exe

# 15.4 Delta Watcom build (_W suffix)
!OUT/delta154/*.EXE
!OUT/delta154/*.exe

# SDK example doors under <version>/bins/ — Clark's own samples linked
# against the PCBKBC libraries, the proof the SDK builds end to end.
# NOT shipping binaries; program EXEs sit at the version top level.
!OUT/*/bins/**/*.EXE
!OUT/*/bins/**/*.exe

# Toolkit libraries: the PCBKBC/PCBKIT/PCBKMS SDK and the category
# libraries, plus their TLIB module listings (*.LST — otherwise caught by
# the `*.lst` scratch rule above).
!toolkit/**/lib/*.LIB
!toolkit/**/lib/*.lib
!toolkit/**/lib/*.LST
!toolkit/**/lib/*.lst
!toolkit/**/lib/*.386
!toolkit/**/obj/*.OBJ
!toolkit/**/obj/*.obj

# Clark's prebuilt MD5 object for the OS/2 build. PCBOARD2.MAK has
# referenced md5.obj since forever while the object existed nowhere in the
# tree; recovered 2026-09-17 from devtools/Md5.zip. Source material, not
# build output, so *.OBJ must not hide it.
!pcb153/SOURCE/MISC/MD5/OS2/*.OBJ
!pcb153/SOURCE/MISC/MD5/OS2/*.obj

# SDK build output: OUT/<branch>/SDK/<compiler>/ -- the libraries we build
# (VMDATA_L.LIB, the category libraries and the PCBKBC/PCBKIT/PCBKMS door
# SDK), their TLIB module listings, and the sample doors linked against
# them. These exist only after a build. They stay visible on purpose: if
# git shows them, we can tell what has been built and whether a
# `make CLEAN` is needed. Added 2026-09-22 with the first built library.
!OUT/*/SDK/**/*.LIB
!OUT/*/SDK/**/*.lib
!OUT/*/SDK/**/*.386
!OUT/*/SDK/**/*.LST
!OUT/*/SDK/**/*.lst
!OUT/*/SDK/**/*.EXE
!OUT/*/SDK/**/*.exe

# PCBIC v1.2 binaries, at the path they are actually in: OUT/upd154/PWA153/.
# The older rule says OUT/pwa153/upd154/, which is not where they live, so
# they were invisible to git.
!OUT/upd154/**/*.EXE
!OUT/upd154/**/*.exe

# Prebuilt category libraries kept in the attic for reference (.386).
!attic/prebuilt-libs/**/*.386

# Program binaries built by BLDDOS: they land directly in OUT/<branch>/,
# e.g. OUT/PWA153/PCBSETUP.EXE. The SDK rule above only reaches
# OUT/<branch>/SDK/, and the OUT/upd154 rule only that one branch, so
# these were invisible to git. Added 2026-09-22 with the first two
# programs that linked: PCBSETUP.EXE and FIDOUTIL.EXE.
!OUT/*/*.EXE
!OUT/*/*.exe
